  <diagram id="auction-semantics" name="Semantics and OCL bindings">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1840" dy="1500" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1840" pageHeight="1500" background="#FFFFFF">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="notes_title" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;AUCTION / semantic contract and source trace&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=29;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="30" width="1750" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ownership_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="115" width="850" height="295" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ownership" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;1 / Goal reliance and actor association&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;auction = AND(start, bid, decide), all within Auction.&lt;br&gt;mAuctioneer = {start, decide}; mParticipant = {bid}.&lt;br&gt;participates-in describes Role-to-Organization association only.&lt;br&gt;Three Goal Dependencies express who is expected to achieve the goals.&lt;br&gt;Each has an external dependum and two directed D-marked legs.&lt;br&gt;Auction&#39;s child goals are depender elements; they have no refinements&lt;br&gt;of their own. Role-side dependee goals may be refined into Tasks.&lt;br&gt;Dependency failure is possible and does not make the notation invalid." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="67" y="135" width="806" height="255" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plans_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="935" y="115" width="860" height="395" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="plans" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;2 / Jason task mapping&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;start&lt;/b&gt;: makeArtifact; focus; start(Service). ASL 19-25.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;decide&lt;/b&gt;: ?focusing(...); stop. ASL 27-30.&lt;br&gt;The query retrieves the existing focus; it does not refocus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;bid&lt;/b&gt;: lookupArtifact; focus; if random &amp;lt; 0.9, wait and bid;&lt;br&gt;otherwise .fail. ASL 32-42. The code says 0.9; its 80% comment is stale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;org-obedient.asl calls goalAchieved only after !Goal succeeds.&lt;br&gt;A successful bid need not improve best_bid or become winner.&lt;br&gt;AuctionArtifact.stop publishes currentWinner, including no_winner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The AND task refinements show the necessary successful plan steps.&lt;br&gt;The .fail branch is not modeled as an alternative achievement." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="957" y="135" width="816" height="355" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="conditions_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="440" width="850" height="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="conditions" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;3 / Thesis extended iStar: evaluating the goals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Section IV-A / Fig. 4 / Table I: refinement and dependency values&lt;br&gt;are propagated; leaf Conditions bind execution to the shared state.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The organizational children now obtain achievement via dependencies.&lt;br&gt;They are not additionally assigned self.*SatisfiedAt &amp;gt;= 0 conditions.&lt;br&gt;A MOISE administrative state must not override a failed actual-bid&lt;br&gt;dependency in the goal model.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Setup/query leaf Tasks: pre = step.enabled; post = step.succeeded.&lt;br&gt;Artifact-call Tasks: source operation contracts plus observed success.&lt;br&gt;step is keyed by scheme run, role player and invocation.&lt;br&gt;Goals use Achieve within one run; MOISE performance is a separate type.&lt;br&gt;A successful protocol run need not achieve every normative iStar goal." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="67" y="460" width="806" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="monitor_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="935" y="540" width="860" height="455" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="monitor" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;4 / Explicit observer interface for the OCL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AuctionMonitor is a required trace projection, not a Java source class.&lt;br&gt;One instance per scheme run / auction Id. Integer times are in ms&lt;br&gt;on one clock; -1 means the event has not occurred.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Consolas&quot;&gt;now&lt;br&gt;startSatisfiedAt, bidEnabledAt, bidSatisfiedAt&lt;br&gt;decideEnabledAt, decideSatisfiedAt : Integer&lt;br&gt;bidCommittedBy, bidDoneBy, actualBidBy : Set(String)&lt;br&gt;adminBidOverride : Boolean&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Satisfied/enabled times come from MOISE, not artifact return times.&lt;br&gt;bidDoneBy comes from done(Sch,bid,Ag); actualBidBy from successful&lt;br&gt;bid calls, including non-winning bids. Do not infer either from winner.&lt;br&gt;bidCommittedBy is frozen at the first bid satisfaction (current before it).&lt;br&gt;adminBidOverride records only an observed successful admin command.&lt;br&gt;These fields audit scheme status; they do not define normative goal values." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="957" y="560" width="816" height="415" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="deadlines_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="830" width="850" height="415" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="deadlines" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;5 / Deadline and recovery semantics&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;bid: ttf = 10000 ms. decide: ttf = 3600000 ms. OS 34-35.&lt;br&gt;Use each obligation&#39;s activation/deadline from MOISE, including&lt;br&gt;a later mission commitment; do not time from MAS startup.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AuctionObligation: one record per bid/decide obligation activation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Consolas&quot;&gt;goal : String  -- bid or decide&lt;br&gt;activatedAt, deadlineAt, endedAt : Integer&lt;br&gt;unfulfilled : Boolean; monitor : AuctionMonitor&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;endedAt = first terminal engine time (fulfilled/unfulfilled/inactive),&lt;br&gt;or -1 while pending. Use engine times, not notification receipt times.&lt;br&gt;unfulfilled remains true after oblUnfulfilled; never erase the record.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WithinDeadline is a conformance norm: pending overtime also fails.&lt;br&gt;Admin recovery allows progress but does not repair an expired duty.&lt;br&gt;Thus the scheme can finish while the iStar bidding goal is unachieved." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="67" y="850" width="806" height="375" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources_panel" parent="1" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1.2;strokeColor=#ADB8C3;fillColor=#F8FAFC;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="935" y="1025" width="860" height="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" parent="1" value="&lt;b&gt;6 / Verified references and scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Local JaCaMo examples/auction:&lt;br&gt;src/org/auction-os.xml: 14-24, 28-50.&lt;br&gt;src/agt/auction_capabilities.asl: 19-42, 53-57.&lt;br&gt;src/env/auction_env/AuctionArtifact.java: 18-44.&lt;br&gt;Resolved moise-1.1.jar: asl/org-obedient.asl;&lt;br&gt;Scheme.isSatisfied and SchemeBoard.admCommand.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/html/1605.07767&quot;&gt;iStar 2.0 Language Guide&lt;/a&gt;: sections 2, 3, 5, 6.1, 6.2, 8.&lt;br&gt;Supplied thesis PDF: section IV-A, Fig. 4, Table I (page 3).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ASL 53-57 handles oblUnfulfilled with goalSatisfied(bid).&lt;br&gt;No blacklist task is added: the source contains only a TODO.&lt;br&gt;Bid Dependency is instantiated per committed Participant enactment;&lt;br&gt;normal global completion requires all such agents, not one winning bid." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="957" y="1045" width="816" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes_footer" parent="1" value="Standard iStar has no generic Goal-to-Goal Association. Cross-actor reliance uses Dependency; mission trace annotations are not semantic edges. The unchanged OCL audits sequence, evidence and deadlines, including administrative recovery; it does not erase normative dependency failure." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="1400" width="1750" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
